    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d176-a1">

                <pb facs="0309" n="303" sameAs="frus:frus1901China/pg303"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure No. 1. Dispatch No.
                        156.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Rockhill to the
                            Chinese Plenipotentiaries.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Commissioner of the United States to China</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1901-08-27"><hi rendition="#italic">August
                                27, 1901</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Your Highness and Your Excellency</hi>: On the 1st of
                    last July I had the honor to communicate to you the earnest desire of my
                    Government to see rehabilitated the memory of Chang Yin-huan, late minister of
                    His Imperial Majesty the Emperor of China to the United States, who was put to
                    death last year in Turkestan.</p>
                <p>Not having heard from your highness and your excellency on the subject, I have
                    the honor to recall the matter, in which my Government takes great interest, to
                    your attention, and would deem it a great personal favor if His Majesty’s
                    Government could be communicated with by telegraph on the subject.</p>
                <p>Hoping that I may promptly be in a position to inform my Government that its wish
                    has been complied with, I avail myself of this opportunity to renew to your
                    highness and your excellency the expression of my highest consideration.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. W. Rockhill</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
